{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016qMfM4T4SKrNctgt7k5ieT","type":"tool_result","content":"+++ b/docs/test/test-cases.toml\n+method = \"\"\"The verdict record's two halves, each driven beside its opposite so neither reads as a \nrule with one answer. THE IDENTITY, pure over synthetic `git ls-tree -r` entries: a listing and the \nsame listing plus a round file, a log fragment and a session log fold EQUAL, while a changed work \nblob and a changed docs/work/ spec each fold DIFFERENT - so the exclusion is proven to be an \nexclusion rather than a fold that ignores everything. THE ENCODING BOUNDARY, driven through git \nrather than asserted about it: a record path holding a non-ASCII character - the shape git QUOTES, \nasserted in the fixture so it cannot silently stop reproducing - leaves the identity unmoved, while \nan accented WORK path moves it; and raw listings with one blob renamed from invalid-UTF-8 path byte \n200 to 201 - asserted to COLLIDE under replacement decoding - fold DIFFERENT through tree_identity, \nso parsing and the ASCII record-prefix boundary occur before any decode. THE TRAILER GRAMMAR: \nformat/parse round-trip; the LAST trailer in a message governs, so a rework commit quoting the \nround it answers does not have the quotation read as its own attestation; and three malformed \nshapes - a verdict word outside the enum, a 40-hex tree, a missing round count - each fail to PARSE \nrather than parse to something. THE NAME PARSE: a round file with and without the relaxed tag, the \npre-train flat layout, a session log, and the legacy hand-authored rollup answering None because it \nnames no reviewed sha. THE GATE, on a two-branch git fixture with the trunk checked out: a logged \nreviewer round naming the current tree clears it with NO rollup present anywhere; the same file \nwith a BUILD session log behind it does not (the implementer-authored round); a SECOND round file \ncommitted behind that ONE session log